Leetcode(235): Finding the Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) of two given nodes in a Binary Search Tree.
- Approach
The key advantage here is the BST property:
If both p and q are greater than the current node, move to the right subtree.
If both are smaller than the current node, move to the left subtree.
Otherwise, the current node is the Lowest Common Ancestor.
I implemented this using an iterative approach, avoiding recursion and making use of the BST structure.

Time Complexity: O(h) 
Space Complexity: O(1)

- Key Takeaway:
The biggest takeaway from today's problem:
Always use the properties of the data structure to optimize your solution.
Instead of traversing the entire tree, the BST property allows us to decide the direction at every step.

